  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe 2D Contour arc fit is now one-sided on a wall walk that knows its part side. The fit does not pass a vertex on the part side by more than 1e-3 mm. The verifier forgives 0.01 mm (`GOUGE_TOL`), so a coarse fit (tolerance 0.1) on a tessellated round wall now verifies clean in both walk directions.\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/arc_side.rs` (new): `sided`, `one_sided`, `air_side_holds`, `splits_on_circle`, `ARC_SIDE_SLACK` = 1e-3 mm, `ARC_SIDE_LOOKAHEAD` = 4.\n- `fit_arcs_sided(pts, tol, air_left)`. Contour, contour chain, the lead reseat and the compensation part contour use it. `fit_arcs` (two-sided) does not change for other callers.\n- When the two-sided circle keeps every vertex within 1e-3 mm of the air side, the fit keeps that circle. Thus a true circle (a hole, a bore, the M8 boss) posts as before. Only a vertex past the slack moves the centre (an open run) or refuses the arc (a closing ring).\n- A sweep over half a turn posts as pieces that end on interior vertices. In a sided fit each split vertex must be within the slack of the circle. Without this check, the conventional walk posted a piece that ended 0.05 mm off its circle, and verify held it as a gouge.\n- A sided fit looks past up to 4 refused run ends before the run ends. Without this, the Ø30 fixture fit 22 (climb) and 32 (conventional) short arcs. With it, each level fits 3 arcs in both directions.\n\nThis continues the held work of commit af47a6ea8 on the same branch. That commit used a slack of 1e-9, and seven golden tests failed. The maintainer's session decided that golden output does not change. No golden, snapshot or test expectation changes in this PR.\n\n`contour_comp` uses the sided fit too. The control offsets that part contour by the register. Thus a part-side sag of it cuts past the wall in the same way, and the verifier reads only the centre moves. The contour walks the centre ring's way round, so its air side is also `climb`. All compensation suites pass unchanged.\n\n`crates/ui/src/law_tests.rs::arc_moves_draw_curved` goes back to `climb: true`, as the issue's \"Done means\" asks. Its assertions do not change.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1579-arc-fit-one-sided.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `contour_arc_fit_wall::coarse_arc_fit_on_a_round_wall_verifies_clean_both_ways` (app). It runs both walk directions: no verify warnings, arcs present, and each arc move ends on its own circle within 1e-3 mm. It fails on main (`climb=true`: `Gouge { at: 3 }` ... `Gouge { at: 11 }`).\n- `arcs::a_sided_fit_never_passes_a_vertex_on_the_part_side` (motion). The worst part-side excursion is 0 mm in both directions (the two-sided fit: 0.04 mm).\n- `law_tests::path_tests::arc_moves_draw_curved` (ui) on the climb walk.\n\nGolden tests that pass unchanged:\n- `contour_bore_arc_entry_matches_golden`, `contour_disc_hole_matches_golden`, `contour_tangential_lead_matches_golden`\n- `every_depth_law_golden_verifies_exactly_as_before`, `every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes`, `a_lead_on_the_rings_own_circle_is_refused`\n- `an_external_m8_thread_verifies_clean_and_posts_helical_moves`\n\nSuites run (debug, all pass):\n- camcraft-motion: `--lib` and the 45 suites that the quick gate plan names for `motion::machining2d`.\n- camcraft-app: the 43 suites of the quick gate plan, plus `conformance`, `altmill_machines`, `per_op_files`, `carvera_post`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The whole `camcraft-ui --lib` suite. Only `arc_moves_draw_curved` ran.\n- The release heavy lanes and the pixel snapshots.\n- A hand test in the GUI.\n\nChangelog: 2D Contour arcs at a coarse tolerance no longer pass a vertex on the part side, so a tessellated round wall verifies clean in both walk directions (#1579)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation; continued from a released claim)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1579\n",
